From 4ae25d92e7aac4d32b9a5b3a1005e6d98678a81b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ynwang <ynwang@iis.u-tokyo.ac.jp>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:02:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] XSpectra GPU step 2: device-resident Lanczos recursion
 and S^-1

- lanczos_acc.f90 (GPU build only): lanczos_acc / lanczos_uspp_acc keep
  the Lanczos vectors on the device for the whole recursion; h_psi, S^-1
  and the axpy/scal/dot operations run there, only a(i), b(i) return to
  the host (convergence test unchanged). Same recursion and order of
  operations as the host routines.
- lr_sm1_psi.f90: the k-point BB_ matrix moves from a SAVEd local of
  sm1_psi_k into module xs_sm1_data (built by sm1_build_bb_k, code moved
  verbatim, host arithmetic unchanged); new sm1_psi_acc applies S^-1 on
  the device with cuBLAS (MYZGEMM), mirroring BB_ when it is rebuilt.
- lanczos.f90: in the GPU build lanczos/lanczos_uspp dispatch to the
  device versions; the host code is otherwise the original (replaces the
  step-1 host/device copies around h_psi).
Small SiO2 test (9 at., 8 k): a,b agree with CPU to <=3.2e-12 over the
first 50 iterations.
